// PositionComputed Group-level computed fields, resolved at query time from live prices and the current macro blend state; never stored. `valuePln` = Σ over the asset's priced subassets; `unitsTotal`/`pricePln`/`priceNative` describe the primary subasset; `profitPct`, `avgBuyPricePln`, `avgBuyPriceNative`, `equivalentUnits` and `costlessSubassets` are the asset-level cost group (task 161): they read the SUM of the recorded costs (`totalSpentPln > 0`) over all subassets of the asset — never a single row's cost and never the stored `avgBuyPrice` — and are all null (or omitted) when no cost is recorded. Every field is optional/nullable; a client treats an absent field as null.
type PositionComputed struct {
	// AvgBuyPriceNative The entry price in the PRIMARY subasset's own `priceCurrency`: `avgBuyPricePln / fx` where fx is the CURRENT PLN rate of that currency (the same rate `priceNative = pricePln / fx` uses) = `priceNative / (1 + profitPct)`. The PLN cost is fixed, so this line moves with the current exchange rate by design (owner rule: "the average price in USD is the PLN average divided by the current dollar rate"). Equals `avgBuyPricePln` when `priceCurrency` is PLN. Null whenever `avgBuyPricePln` is null (Σcost ≤ 0, unpriced primary) or the FX rate is unavailable. Not stored. Never derived from the stored `avgBuyPrice`.
	AvgBuyPriceNative *float64 `json:"avgBuyPriceNative,omitempty"`

	// AvgBuyPricePln The asset's ENTRY PRICE in PLN per 1 unit of the PRIMARY subasset: `pricePln / (1 + profitPct)` = `Σcost / (Σvalue / pricePln)`, so `avgBuyPricePln × equivalentUnits = Σcost` and `pricePln / avgBuyPricePln − 1 = profitPct`. Equivalence of non-primary holdings is measured at today's prices (no history). Derived from the recorded costs; NOT computed from the stored `avgBuyPrice` and NOT `avgBuyPrice × fxRate`. Null whenever `profitPct` is null, when the primary is unpriced, or when `profitPct` is −1. Changing the primary re-expresses the same cost in the new primary's terms (`entry(P′) / entry(P) = price(P′) / price(P)`). Not stored.
	AvgBuyPricePln *float64 `json:"avgBuyPricePln,omitempty"`

	// CostlessSubassets Tickers (`Subasset.ticker`) of the asset's priced subassets that hold units but have no recorded cost (`totalSpentPln` null or ≤ 0), listed only when an entry price is computed (Σcost > 0). Their baseline is assumed to sit inside a sibling's group-level cost — the known limitation of the entry price: a subasset bought without its cost being entered inflates `profitPct` and lowers the entry price. Optional; omitted (or empty) when there are none.
	CostlessSubassets *[]string `json:"costlessSubassets,omitempty"`
	CurrentPct        *float64  `json:"currentPct,omitempty"`

	// DeviationPct `(currentPct / effectiveTargetAllocationPct) − 1`. Uses the same effectiveTargetAllocationPct value below as its denominator — the two fields never disagree about which target is "the" target.
	//
	// Exception (ADR-053): when effectiveTargetAllocationPct is non-null and exactly 0 while currentPct is > 0 (the asset holds nonzero value against an explicit zero target, e.g. CHFPLN=X after ADR-050 retired it to a 0.0/0.0 risk-on/risk-off target while keeping the row and its holding), the formula above is undefined (division by zero) and this field instead returns a fixed sentinel, 1.0. Any holding at all against a hard zero target is unambiguously in excess, so a constant flag value is used rather than an unbounded number that would scale with how much is held — the severity signal here is binary (hold something → flag it), not continuous. 1.0 was chosen because it renders as a clean, bounded "+100%" in a naive `(deviationPct * 100).toFixed(0)` display and safely exceeds the 0.5 "SELL" threshold `frontend-web` uses. Assets with a null effectiveTargetAllocationPct (null-target assets such as ALGO-USD/FISV/GME) are unaffected and keep this field null, exactly as before.
	DeviationPct *float64 `json:"deviationPct,omitempty"`

	// EffectiveTargetAllocationPct The target allocation actually used for rebalancing right now — i.e. the same value `deviationPct` divides by, exposed as its own field (added 2026-07-06; previously computed internally by PositionService but never surfaced, which is why the UI could show a stale-looking raw target while deviationPct quietly used a different blended number).
	// For a RETIREMENT asset, a MAIN asset when `rebalancing.macro_derisk_enabled = false`, or any asset with a null `targetAllocationPct`: this equals `targetAllocationPct` exactly (null stays null — it is never coerced to 0, even though the internal macro-override map does that substitution elsewhere for bookkeeping reasons that must not leak into this field).
	// For a MAIN asset with a non-null `targetAllocationPct` while the gate is enabled: `riskOff × (1 − blendFactor) + riskOn × blendFactor`, where `riskOn` = `targetAllocationPct`, `riskOff` = `targetAllocationPctRiskOff` (falling back to `riskOn` when null), and `blendFactor` is the latest `GET /market-data/macro-state` value (0 = full risk-off, 1 = full risk-on — orientation flipped by ADR-071; a missing macro_state row is treated as `blendFactor = 1`, i.e. full risk-on — identical to today's `targetAllocationPct`; was `blendFactor = 0` under the original ADR-044 orientation).
	EffectiveTargetAllocationPct *float64 `json:"effectiveTargetAllocationPct,omitempty"`

	// EquivalentUnits Primary-equivalent units `valuePln / pricePln`: what the asset's holdings in ALL subassets are worth today in units of the primary (0.12 BTC for 0.1 BTC plus an ETN worth 0.02 BTC). The quantity the entry price averages the cost over: `avgBuyPricePln × equivalentUnits = Σcost`. Optional; present whenever the primary is priced (independent of whether any cost is recorded), null otherwise.
	EquivalentUnits *float64 `json:"equivalentUnits,omitempty"`

	// PriceNative pricePln converted back to the primary subasset's native priceCurrency via the current FX rate. Null whenever pricePln or the FX rate is unavailable.
	PriceNative *float64 `json:"priceNative,omitempty"`
	PricePln    *float64 `json:"pricePln,omitempty"`

	// ProfitPct Asset-level profit as a fraction (0.1 = +10 %): `Σvalue / Σcost − 1`, where Σcost = Σ `totalSpentPln` over the asset's subassets whose `totalSpentPln` is > 0, and Σvalue = Σ `effectiveUnits × pricePln` over EVERY priced subasset, including those with no recorded cost (the go-live import stored the whole group's cost on the head row, so a cost-less wrapper's value belongs to the same cost). A subasset with a recorded cost but no price contributes neither its cost nor a value. Null when Σcost ≤ 0 (no cost recorded — e.g. every portfolioB asset today) or when the primary is unpriced. Independent of which subasset is primary. Computed identically for MAIN and RETIREMENT assets (ADR-104, 2026-10-18, lifted ADR-056's RETIREMENT null-out once RETIREMENT's reviewed cost baselines existed).
	ProfitPct  *float64 `json:"profitPct,omitempty"`
	UnitsTotal *float64 `json:"unitsTotal,omitempty"`
	ValuePln   *float64 `json:"valuePln,omitempty"`
}

